  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 759583,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 13th (Commodore 64) - Synopsis\n\nSurvive the night in *13th*, a chilling horror adventure for the Commodore 64! You are one of five camp counselors tasked with protecting a group of children from the relentless pursuit of Jason Voorhees. This isn't a straightforward action game; much of your time is spent cautiously navigating the dark, wooded paths surrounding Camp Crystal Lake. \n\nResource management is key. Scavenge for rocks, knives, and other makeshift weapons to defend yourself and the children from the undead hordes that roam the forest.  Jason himself is a terrifying presence, appearing sporadically to challenge your courage and skill. Combat is deliberate and tense, demanding careful planning and strategic use of your limited resources. \n\n*13th* blends exploration, puzzle-solving, and survival horror, creating a uniquely unsettling experience. Can you keep the children safe and escape the clutches of Jason Voorhees before dawn? Your survival depends on it!"
    },
